<title>FRANCE: Dublin summit decisive step to 1999 euro - Trichet.</title>
<headline>Dublin summit decisive step to 1999 euro - Trichet.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of France governor Jean-Claude Trichet said on Tuesday that the European Union summit in Dublin last weekend had marked a decisive step towards ensuring the move to the euro single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;The advance towards a single currency was decisively confirmed at the European summit in Dublin where an agreement was reached on the legal status of the euro, the new European monetary system and on the stability and growth pact intended to guarantee fiscal discipline in the monetary union,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
</text>
